
Contents of "cnet:mail/"

    JamCall.rexx

        - My version of an "intelligent" dialer script for Jam-Mail. There
          are still some problems and things it doesn't check for, but it
          DOES work, and shouldn't cause you to lose data, connections, etc.

        - If ANYONE has any insights into dialing out with Jam-Mail, please
          send me your scripts, so I can LEARN from them. Thanks!

    Poll-Script1

        - Creates initial poll output window and launches main poll script.

    Poll-Script2

        - This is the main polling script. Take a look through it and change
          anything you think needs to be for your system setup. All other
          support files are launched from this script(eg: the tick, nodediff,
          etc. scripts, as well as the dialer above, JamScan and CNet TOSS.)

Other Files: (Not included with this archive):

    jamscan.cfg

        - Used with the "JamScan" file, this is the config file used to tell
          which packets should be checked for and packed even further than
          CNet's Toss file does. The main polling script above runs JamScan
          right before Toss is run BEFORE dialing your boss node.

    xfreq.cfg

        - This config file is used to launch your Freq processor. I am still
          playing with getting "FReqMate" running under Jam-Scan, so this
          file was not included yet until I get the kinks worked out in my
          Freq setup.

